{"id":"brazil-cities","title":"Largest cities in Brazil","prompt":"Name the 10 most populous cities in Brazil (2025 estimates)","noun":"cities","category":"Geography","metric":"Population (2025 est.)","blitz":true,"source":{"name":"Wikipedia: List of cities in Brazil by population","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_cities_in_Brazil_by_population","asOf":"2026-11-08","dataAsOf":"2025"},"answers":[{"rank":1,"name":"São Paulo","aliases":["São Paul","Sao Paulo, Brazil","Sao Paolo","San Paulo","São Paulo City","São Paulo-SP","City of São Paulo","Sao Pablo","Sao palo","Sao Paolo, Brazil","Saint Paul, Brazil","SP","Sampa"],"value":"11,904,961","n":11904961,"article":"São Paulo","fact":{"text":"Capital of São Paulo state, it is home to the largest Arab, Italian and Japanese diasporas in the world.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A3o_Paulo"}},{"rank":2,"name":"Rio de Janeiro","aliases":["Rio de Janeiro, Brazil","Rio de Janiero","Rio de janerio","São Sebastião do Rio de Janeiro","Rio de Janero","River of January","January River","City of Rio de Janeiro","R. Janeiro","Rio de Janeiro, RJ","Rio di Janeiro","Río de Jeneiro","Rio de Janeiro city","Rio Janeiro","Rio, Brazil","BRRIO","Rio de Janiero, Brazil","Rio de Jainero","Rio","RJ"],"value":"6,730,729","n":6730729,"article":"Rio de Janeiro","fact":{"text":"In Rio de Janeiro state, it hosted the Portuguese court from 1808: the only modern case of a capital moving to a colony.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rio_de_Janeiro"}},{"rank":3,"name":"Brasília","aliases":["Brasilia, Brazil","Brazilia","Capital of brazil","Brasillia","Brazillia","Brazíliaváros","Brasília, DF","Brasilea","Brasilia Distrito Federal"],"value":"2,996,899","n":2996899,"article":"Brasília","fact":{"text":"Brazil's capital, in the Federal District, is laid out like an airplane, with the Monumental Axis as its fuselage.","source":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bras%C3%ADlia"}},{"rank":4,"name":"Fortaleza","aliases":["Fortaleza, Br